# PVC Patterns Rules (English Canonical)

> Korean siblings: `patterns/async-patterns.mdc`, `form-handling.mdc`, `caching-strategy.mdc`.

## 1. Async Patterns

- Prefer `async/await` with explicit error handling; no silent fire-and-forget.
- Use `Promise.all` vs `allSettled` deliberately; prefer `AbortController` for cancellation.
- UI states: `idle | loading | success | error`; prevent double-submit; provide retry; avoid late responses overwriting newer UI.
- Timeouts/retries only when idempotent; don’t empty-catch; don’t block UI thread with huge sync work.

## 2. Form Handling

- Validate at field, form, and **server** layers; never trust client-only checks.
- Accessible labels (not placeholder-only); errors near fields + `aria-invalid`/`aria-describedby`; not color-only.
- Preserve input on network failure; idempotency keys when needed; reuse project form library/patterns.

## 3. Caching

- Correctness over micro-gains; include user/tenant/auth scope in keys; plan TTL/invalidation with every write path.
- Authenticated responses: `private` cache; don’t CDN-share user-specific data.
- After mutations, invalidate/update related lists/details; never long-term cache raw secrets.
